<title>ITALY: Ciampi talking about Italian not EU lira committee.</title>
<headline>Ciampi talking about Italian not EU lira committee.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi was referring to Italy's own euro committee and not the European Union monetary committee when referring to work on the re-entry of the lira to the ERM.</p>
<p>Asked by reporters about progress towards putting the lira back into the European exchange rate mechanism (ERM), Ciampi answered: &quot;The monetary committee has started to work and the work is going well.&quot;</p>
<p>A Treasury spokesman later said Ciampi was referring to the Italian euro committee. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
